'In Russia, they believe that it is necessary to further escalate the situation to show Europe where Russia's red lines are,' – Wanner.

'There is one piece of information I would like to share. A few days ago, I spoke with representatives of the Russian Ministry of Foreign Affairs. These were not top-level officials, but rather representatives of the second and third tiers, who can be described as relatively moderate. However, their moods alarmed me. They said that in the confrontation with Ukraine and the West, it is necessary to further escalate the situation to show Western Europe where Russia's red lines are. I heard statements about the need to strike at military-industrial complex enterprises in Western Europe that are helping Ukraine. Some even mentioned the possibility of using tactical nuclear weapons. As for whether such views are shared by the Russian president and the country's top leadership, I cannot assess that.'

@Slavyangrad
